# SHA-256 of workshop/site/hackathon.html: the freeze baseline for AC21 (specs/005-teaching-spa.md).
# The page stays byte-identical until workshop/spa/docs/hackathon-retired.md exists. A rehearsal
# record, passing or failing, does not release it.
#
# The digest is of the exact bytes on disk (199769 bytes, LF); tests/spa/hackathon-untouched.test.ts
# hashes the page as read, with no line-ending normalization. .gitattributes pins the page with
# -text, so every checkout, on any OS, holds the committed bytes. A worktree created before that
# line landed keeps a stale CRLF copy until the page is re-checked-out:
#   git checkout -- workshop/site/hackathon.html   (after deleting the file)
# Do not edit the digest to make a checkout pass. To reproduce:
#   PowerShell: (Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 workshop/site/hackathon.html).Hash
#   POSIX:      sha256sum workshop/site/hackathon.html
0fc164d64b5f03ccb76256f876641026297a35c14e10c6c73b15a74aea9a61cb
